      "user": 1,
      "prompt": "What is Django?",
      "response": "Django is a free and open-source web framework written in Python. It is a high-level framework that enables rapid development of secure, maintainable, and scalable websites. Django is often referred to as a \"batteries included\" framework because it provides a lot of functionality out of the box, such as:\n\n1. A modular design that allows you to easily add or remove components as needed.\n2. A built-in ORM (Object-Relational Mapping) system that abstracts the underlying database, making it easy to work with different databases.\n3. A template engine that allows you to separate presentation logic from application logic.\n4. Support for internationalization and localization (i18n and L10n).\n5. Support for testing and debugging.\n6. A built-in administration interface that allows you to manage models, views, and other data.\n7. Support for caching, session management, and other common web development tasks.\n\nDjango is designed to make it easy to build robust, secure, and maintainable websites quickly. It provides a lot of built-in functionality, making it a good choice for building complex web applications. However, it is also flexible and can be used to build simple web applications as well.\n\nSome of the key features of Django include:\n\n* **Modular design**: Django is designed to be modular, allowing you to easily add or remove components as needed.\n* **ORM system**: Django's ORM system abstracts the underlying database, making it easy to work with different databases.\n* **Template engine**: Django's template engine allows you to separate presentation logic from application logic.\n* **Auto-discovery**: Django's auto-discovery feature allows you to automatically discover and configure models, views, and other components.\n* **Built-in administration interface**: Django provides a built-in administration interface that allows you to manage models, views, and other data.\n* **Support for testing and debugging**: Django provides built-in support for testing and debugging, making it easy to write and run tests for your application.\n\nOverall, Django is a powerful and flexible web framework that is well-suited for building complex web applications.",
      "created_at": "2026-09-24T15:45:28.942Z"
    }
  },
