      "user": 1,
      "prompt": "tell me about python full stack in shorter words\n",
      "response": "Python Full Stack refers to the ability to handle all layers of web development using the Python programming language. Here's a breakdown:\n\n**Front-end:** HTML, CSS, JavaScript, and frameworks like React or Angular for creating user interfaces.\n\n**Back-end:** Python is used to create the server-side logic, API connectivity, and database interactions. Frameworks like Django, Flask, or Pyramid help with this.\n\n**Database:** Python can interact with various databases like MySQL, PostgreSQL, MongoDB, or SQLite to store and retrieve data.\n\n**Full Stack:** With Python, you can handle all these layers, from front-end to back-end, and even database interactions, making it a versatile and powerful language for web development.",
